## Summary

This is the OfficeFloor arm of a PetClinic variant. The single write endpoint is `POST /api/owners`, implemented as a YAML-defined chain of small function classes. Note a key finding up front: the existing test expects a `GOLD` tier for a 3-member household, but the current `membershipTier` computation only ever produces `SILVER` or `BRONZE` — there is no GOLD logic and no repository method to count household members.

---

## 1. membershipTier — definition, setting, and BRONZE/SILVER rules

It is a derived (computed) field, not stored on the entity. It is produced in the MapStruct mapper when converting `Owner` -> `OwnerDto`.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` line 24 (full computation, verbatim):

```java
24	    @Mapping(target = "membershipTier", expression = "java(owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0 && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \"SILVER\" : \"BRONZE\")")
```

Rule: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` AND `email` is non-null/non-blank; otherwise `BRONZE`. There is NO `GOLD` branch anywhere.

The field itself is defined on the generated `OwnerDto` (generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec — no hand-written `.java` exists). Spec definition at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2098-2103:

```yaml
2098	            membershipTier:
2099	              title: Membership tier
2100	              description: The owner's membership tier. 'SILVER' when namesakeCount is 0 and an email is present, otherwise 'BRONZE'.
2101	              type: string
2102	              readOnly: true
2103	              example: 'SILVER'
```

The inputs it depends on are set earlier in the POST chain:
- `namesakeCount` is set by `CountNamesakes` (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CountNamesakes.java`), which iterates `ownerRepository.findAll()` counting existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), then `owner.setNamesakeCount(count)` (lines 15-26).
- `email` comes from the request via `BuildOwner` -> `ownerMapper.toOwner(request)`.

---

## 2. householdId — definition on the Owner entity/DTO

Entity field at `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` lines 60-61, with accessors at 117-123:

```java
