121	    public void setHouseholdId(String householdId) {
122	        this.householdId = householdId;
123	    }
```

DTO side (generated `OwnerDto` from OpenAPI), `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` lines 2110-2115 — read-only output field. The request-only opt-in flag `sharesHousehold` is defined on `OwnerFields` (generated `OwnerFieldsDto`) at lines 2047-2052 (`writeOnly: true`, not stored/returned).

`householdId` is assigned during create by `AssignHousehold` (see below).

---

## 3. Owner CREATE endpoint (POST /owners)

YAML flow definition: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` (full content, 66 lines). The chain is:

`validate` -> `checkTelephone` -> `checkHousehold` -> `checkCityCapacity` -> `checkDailyLimit` -> `build` -> `assignCode` -> `assignHousehold` -> `countNamesakes` -> `save` -> `audit` -> `checkBulkSignup` -> `respond`

Each step names a function class in `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner`. Guarded by `authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"` and `govern: [ transaction ]`.

Java function classes backing the create flow (all under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`):

- `ValidateOwner.java`
- `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique.java`
- `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java`
- `CheckOwnerCityCapacity.java`
- `CheckOwnerDailyLimit.java`
- `BuildOwner.java`
- `AssignCustomerCode.java` (referenced as `assignCode`)
- `AssignHousehold.java`
- `CountNamesakes.java`
- `SaveOwner.java`
- `AuditOwnerCreated.java`
- `CheckBulkSignup.java`
- `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`

Household-relevant classes, verbatim highlights:

`BuildOwner.java` (lines 11-17): maps request to `Owner` and sets registration date to effective business day.

`AssignHousehold.java` (lines 22-33) — sets `householdId`:
```java
22	    public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
23	        if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
24	            OwnerHousehold household = OwnerHousehold.of(owner);
25	            for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
26	                if (existing.getHouseholdId() != null && household.equals(OwnerHousehold.of(existing))) {
27	                    owner.setHouseholdId(existing.getHouseholdId());
28	                    return;
29	                }
