```

`CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java` (lines 20-31): iterates `findAll()`, throws `OwnerHouseholdDuplicateException` on same-household collision unless `sharesHousehold` is true.

`OwnerHousehold.java` (record, lines 20-42): the single "same household" definition = normalized `lastName` + normalized `address` (via `OwnerAddress.normalize`), compared case-insensitively with collapsed whitespace. `of(Owner)` and `of(OwnerFieldsDto)` factories.

---

## OwnerRepository methods available

Interface `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`:

- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)` (line 46)
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable)` (line 48)
- `Owner findById(int id)` (line 57)
- `void save(Owner owner)` (line 66)
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()` (line 74)
- `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable)` (line 76)
- `void delete(Owner owner)` (line 84)

There is NO count method and nothing that counts household members. `AssignHousehold`, `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique` and `CountNamesakes` all work by iterating `findAll()` in memory. The Spring Data impl (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`) only overrides the interface methods with `@Query` annotations — no extra query methods (no `countByHouseholdId`, etc.). Other impls: `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`.

---

## 4. Relevant tests

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (full content):

```java
7	/** tier-gold: membershipTier is 'GOLD' when the owner's household has 3+ members after this
8	 * create. Build a shared household (same lastName + address, sharesHousehold) and assert the third
9	 * member is GOLD. */
10	class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
12		@Test
13		void coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold() throws Exception {
14			String lastName = uniqueLastName();
15			String address = uniqueAddress();
16			for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
17				ObjectNode m = ownerNode();
18				m.put("lastName", lastName);
19				m.put("address", address);
20				m.put("sharesHousehold", true);
21				createOwnerOk(m);
22			}
23			ObjectNode third = ownerNode();
24			third.put("lastName", lastName);
25			third.put("address", address);
26			third.put("sharesHousehold", true);
27			int id = createOwnerOk(third);
28			getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.membershipTier").value("GOLD"));
29		}
30	}
```

This test expects `GOLD` when a household reaches 3+ members, but no such rule is currently implemented (the mapper only yields SILVER/BRONZE, and no repository method counts household members).

Supporting base class `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` (322 lines): `@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN...)`. Key helpers: `ownerNode()` builds a fully-unique valid owner (firstName "Test", unique lastName/address/city/telephone — note: no email by default, line 117-125); `createOwnerOk(body)` POSTs and returns the created id; `getOwner(id)` GETs; `uniqueLastName()`/`uniqueAddress()` generate collision-free values. Because `ownerNode()` sets no email, a created owner would be `BRONZE` under the current rule unless email is added.

Also present: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` (test support for the `AuditOwnerCreated` step). I did not find any other tests referencing membershipTier, household, or namesake.

